B.cil=new A.oS("Immunocompromised child","Proper wound management followed by local infiltration of RIG in BOTH Category II and Category III exposures. After this, a complete course of rabies vaccine by the intramuscular route should be undertaken in both Category II and Category III exposures. IAP 2022 states the same principle: RIG/RMAb is also indicated in Category II in immunocompromised patients.",B.bx,B.iI)
B.cig=new A.oS("Pregnancy","No condition, including pregnancy, is a contraindication to post-exposure prophylaxis. It is safe in all age groups.",B.bI,B.oL)
B.cin=new A.oS("A vaccine dose was delayed","Should a vaccine dose be delayed for any reason, the PEP regimen should be resumed or continued \u2014 NOT restarted. Give the missed dose as soon as possible and continue the remaining schedule.",B.bI,B.hW)
B.cio=new A.oS("The vaccine product or route has to change mid-course","Changes in rabies vaccine product and/or the route of administration during the same PEP course are acceptable, if unavoidable, to ensure that the course is completed.",B.bI,B.oL)
B.cij=new A.oS("Multiple wounds","The calculated dose of RIG/RMAb may not be sufficient to infiltrate all wounds. Dilute it in sterile normal saline to a volume sufficient to inject all of them. Distribute by wound size and depth, giving priority to the deepest and most contaminated.",B.bI,B.hW)
B.cim=new A.oS("Previously vaccinated, direct nerve exposure suspected","RIG is not routinely indicated in a previously immunised patient. However, where direct nerve exposure is suspected, the treating physician may consider RIG infiltration. This is a clinician decision, not routine treatment.",B.bx,B.hW)
B.cik=new A.oS("COVID vaccine and rabies vaccine together","Both can be given together at different sites, or at any interval, as both are killed vaccines.",B.bI,B.oL)
B.cih=new A.oS("Routine immunisation status","Rabies post-exposure prophylaxis should be administered irrespective of previous routine vaccination status.",B.bI,B.oL)
B.cii=new A.oS("The child had pre-exposure prophylaxis","Pre-exposure prophylaxis makes administration of RIG unnecessary after a bite. A routine PrEP booster or serology is recommended only where a continued high risk of exposure remains, such as laboratory work with rabies virus.",B.bI,B.oL)
B.cif=new A.oS("Animal availability and observation","Category I requires a RELIABLE contact history before prophylaxis is withheld. Animal observation is a public-health activity that supports assessment; it is not a reason to delay prophylaxis that is otherwise indicated. If the animal is unavailable, has escaped, is behaving abnormally, or is suspected rabid, proceed on the exposure category and seek public-health guidance.",B.bx,B.hW)
B.bFV=s([B.cil,B.cig,B.cin,B.cio,B.cij,B.cim,B.cik,B.cih,B.cii,B.cif],A.af("H<oS>"))
